/--
Source-regularity form of Proposition `uniqueness`.  Interpreting “the score
distributions are twice continuously differentiable within their supports”
as pointwise `C²` regularity of each one-draw lower CDF at every non-origin
represented score, the finite-iid maximum CDF is automatically `C¹`; no
separate smoothness assumption on the producer reward is required.
-/
theorem canonicalTwoUser_nonzeroSupportGenres_eq_singleton_of_scaledNormRpowCostNash_of_phase_scoreCdfContDiffAt
    {P : ℕ} [Nonempty (Fin P)] {α β θ : ℝ} {μ : Measure (Content 2)}
    [IsProbabilityMeasure μ]
    (hP : 1 < P) (hα : 0 < α) (hβ : 1 ≤ β)
