/--
Corrected generic below-phase uniqueness under the precise boundary
non-flatness hypothesis isolated by the C1 proof.  This removes the former
opaque strict-cone premise: acute zero-first-score points are excluded by C1
projection, orthogonal zero-first-score points require positive first reward
derivative at zero, and every lower-ray point requires positive second reward
derivative there.  Raw CDF C2 is still used only for the subsequent graph
argument and does not silently imply either positivity condition.
-/
theorem canonicalTwoUser_nonzeroSupportGenres_eq_singleton_of_scaledNormRpowCostNash_of_phase_of_positiveLowerBoundaryRewardDeriv
    {P : ℕ} [Nonempty (Fin P)] {α β theta : ℝ} {mu : Measure (Content 2)}
